ProjectScale: SDD

Purpose:
  Define project scale levels L0-L5. Scale is one of the primary inputs
  to architecture selection — it determines what patterns, infrastructure,
  and complexity are appropriate. Scale is NOT the only input: team size,
  budget, compliance, and risk also matter.

Owns: ./

Levels:

  L0:
    name: Prototype
    description: Throwaway or exploratory code
    users: < 100
    traffic: negligible
    data: minimal
    team: 1
    budget: minimal
    availability: none
    architecture:
      - single app
      - local DB
      - minimal infrastructure
    applicable:
      - prototypes
      - experiments
      - proof-of-concept

  L1:
    name: Small
    description: Small production system
    users: 100 - 1K
    traffic: < 10 RPS
    data: GB scale
    team: 1-3
    budget: low
    availability: 99%
    architecture:
      - modular application
      - single DB
      - basic cache
      - basic CI/CD
    applicable:
      - internal tools
      - small SaaS
      - MVPs

  L2:
    name: Production
    description: Standard production system
    users: 1K - 100K
    traffic: 10-100 RPS
    data: TB scale
    team: 3-10
    budget: medium
    availability: 99.9%
    architecture:
      - modular architecture
      - HA considerations
      - observability
      - backup
      - security
    applicable:
      - production SaaS
      - business platforms
      - customer-facing apps

  L3:
    name: Large
    description: High-scale production system
    users: 100K - 1M
    traffic: 100-1000 RPS
    data: TB-PB scale
    team: 10-50
    budget: high
    availability: 99.95%
    architecture:
      - high traffic scaling
      - distributed components
      - advanced caching
      - queues
      - multi-region optional
    applicable:
      - high-traffic platforms
      - marketplaces
      - financial systems

  L4:
    name: Critical
    description: Mission-critical system
    users: 1M - 10M
    traffic: 1000-10000 RPS
    data: PB scale
    team: 50-200
    budget: very high
    availability: 99.99%
    architecture:
      - HA multi-zone
      - disaster recovery
      - strong security
      - failure isolation
      - advanced observability
    applicable:
      - payment systems
      - authentication systems
      - regulated systems

  L5:
    name: Massive
    description: Massive scale, mission-critical
    users: 10M+
    traffic: 10000+ RPS
    data: PB+ scale
    team: 200+
    budget: very high
    availability: 99.999%
    architecture:
      - multi-region
      - advanced resilience
      - strict compliance
      - extreme scale
      - custom infrastructure
    applicable:
      - global platforms
      - critical infrastructure
      - government systems

Selection:
  AI MUST calculate ProjectScale from:
    DAU/MAU
    RPS (requests per second)
    Peak RPS
    Concurrent users
    Data volume
    Read/write ratio
    Latency requirements
    Availability requirements
    Team size
    Budget
    Compliance requirements

  ProjectScale is distinct from:
    SecurityLevel (L0-L5 in security/levels.sdd)
    TestLevel (L0-L5 in testing/levels.sdd)
    ArchitecturePattern (modular monolith, microservices, etc.)

  These are independent scales that together determine the architecture.

Navigation:
  Patterns: @patterns.sdd
  Scaling: @scaling.sdd
  Data: @data.sdd
  Availability: @availability.sdd
  Observability: @observability.sdd
  Networking: @networking.sdd
  Deployment: @deployment.sdd
  Project: @project/project.sdd
  ProjectArchitecture: @instances/vkard.az/architecture/INDEX.sdd
  Decisions: @instances/vkard.az/decisions/INDEX.sdd

